            <ArticleTitle>[Policy document. Catheter-based diagnosis and treatment of coronary diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>303-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diagnostic coronary angiography and percutaneous coronary interventions (PCI) are rapidly developing fields. In-house thoracic surgery backup is no longer a prerequisite for PCI. The demand for physicians trained in interventional cardiology has created a need to formalise such education. The Swedish societies of cardiology and thoracic radiology have agreed on a policy document establishing the details of this education. It is the responsibility of the tutor to decide when the pupil has achieved adequate skills.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
